  "id": "COMPOUND:26018 - PROTEIN:1574",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a direct relationship between the compound (1S,2R,6R,7R,8S,10R,13S)-2,7,8-trihydroxy-6,7,13-trimethyl-4,9-dioxatetracyclo[6.5.1.01,10.06,10]tetradecan-3-one and the Interleukin-5 receptor subunit alpha. This relationship is mediated through the enzyme Cytochrome P450 1A2, which is targeted by multiple related compounds, including (2R)-7,4'-Dihydroxy-5-Methoxy-8-Methylflavan and Berkeleyacetal B. These compounds, in turn, are also targeted by Npc174832, a third molecule that ultimately interacts with the Interleukin-5 receptor subunit alpha. The consistent presence of a target relationship across these different compounds, all leading to the same target, indicates a potential mechanism of action involving the enzyme Cytochrome P450 1A2. The evidence suggests that the compound in question may act as a substrate or modulator of this enzyme, thereby influencing the Interleukin-5 receptor subunit alpha. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role in immune regulation, as the Interleukin-5 receptor subunit alpha is critical for immune cell activation and function.",
